IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssaa-claimant`

-- The Minister's and Secretary's instruments under the Social Security (Administration) Act 1999 -- the s 14A class of
-- persons, adequate job search efforts (s 42AC(3)), reasonable excuse (s 42AI), and persistent mutual obligation failures with
-- the half or whole reduction (s 42AR), read from the deposited instruments. A module beside ssaa-claimant.l4; it works out
-- facts that module asks for and calls its questions, restating none of its rules.
--
-- SEAT: the claimant and jobseeker, as in ssaa-claimant.l4.
--
-- Editions, each deposited 2026-10-23 as its own subject with parent_act this Act:
--  * Social Security (Administration) (Class of Persons - Intent to Claim) Determination 2018, as made (F2018L00971), s 14A;
--  * Social Security (Administration) (Job Search Efforts) Determination 2026, as made (F2026L01408, made 21 October 2026),
--    s 42AC(3); it repealed the 2018 determination;
--  * Social Security (Administration) (Reasonable Excuse - Participation Payments) Determination 2018, as made (F2018L00779),
--    ss 42AI(1), (3) (and 42U, not used here);
--  * Social Security (Administration) (Non-Compliance) Determination 2018 (No. 1), Compilation No. 1 (F2022C00591), s 42AR(1).
-- s 42AO(3) (relocation assistance): no instrument is in force; the Relocation Assistance Specification 2014 (F2014L00900) and
-- its predecessors are marked not in force on the Register (title search 23 October 2026). The baseline's input is kept.
--
-- Judgments the instruments leave to the Secretary (the quality of job searches, whether a matter directly prevented compliance,
-- whether to make a s 42AF(2) determination at all) are answered conditionally, never guessed.

§ `Social Security (Administration) instruments -- the jobseeker's questions`

§§ `s 14A, Class of Persons Determination s 5 -- does my claim date back to my first contact`

-- s 5: "a person is in a class of persons if the person is unable to lodge a claim on the contact day because, at any time
-- during the relevant period [the 8 weeks ending on the contact day], the person is: subject to domestic or family violence;
-- homeless; hospitalised or suffering from a temporary incapacity arising from a medical condition; released from prison or
-- psychiatric confinement; experiencing high stress associated with a relationship separation; a parent of a dependent child
-- born during the relevant period; affected by the death during the relevant period of an immediate family member; a person
-- who entered Australia during the relevant period as a humanitarian entrant ...; a person whose usual place of residence is
-- in a remote area, and the person is physically present in the remote area; a person whose principal place of residence was
-- lost or sustained major damage during the relevant period as a result of an extreme circumstance, or subject to other
-- special circumstances beyond the person's control."
DECLARE `My circumstance in the 8 weeks before I made contact` IS ONE OF
    `domestic or family violence`
    `homelessness`
    `hospital, or a temporary incapacity from a medical condition`
    `release from prison or psychiatric confinement`
    `high stress from a relationship separation`
    `a child of mine born in those 8 weeks`
    `the death of an immediate family member in those 8 weeks`
    `arrival in Australia in those 8 weeks as a humanitarian entrant`
    `living in, and being in, a remote area`
    `my home lost or badly damaged in those 8 weeks by flood, fire, earthquake, storm or another extreme event`
    `other special circumstances beyond my control`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `circumstance` IS A `My circumstance in the 8 weeks before I made contact`
      `it stopped me lodging on the day of contact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am in the s 14A class` IF
    (NOT (`circumstance` EQUALS `none of these`)) AND `it stopped me lodging on the day of contact`

@export I contacted Services Australia before lodging my claim. Taking the s 14A class from the Minister's determination, on what day is my claim taken to have been made (ss 13, 14A)?
GIVEN `the day I contacted the Department` IS A DATE @desc The day you (or someone for you) first contacted the Department about the claim
      `the day I lodged the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you actually lodged the claim
      `circumstance` IS A `My circumstance in the 8 weeks before I made contact` @desc Which of these applied to you at any time in the 8 weeks ending on the day of contact, if any
      `it stopped me lodging on the day of contact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that circumstance is why you could not lodge the claim on the day you made contact
      `I was qualified on the day of contact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day of contact, you were already qualified for the payment
      `it is crisis payment or special employment advance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for crisis payment or a special employment advance
      `why late` IS A `Why I lodged late` @desc If you lodged more than 14 days after contact: the reason the Secretary is satisfied delayed you throughout, if any
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day is my claim taken to be made, with the s 14A class` MEANS
    `On what day is my claim taken to be made` `the day I contacted the Department` `the day I lodged the claim` (`I am in the s 14A class` `circumstance` `it stopped me lodging on the day of contact`) `I was qualified on the day of contact` `it is crisis payment or special employment advance` `why late`

§§ `s 42AC(3), Job Search Efforts Determination s 6 -- did I do enough job searching`

-- s 6(1): "the Secretary: (a) must assess whether, during that period, the person made the number of job searches that the
-- person was required to make; and (b) if the person made the required number of job searches -- may do any of the following:
-- (i) assess the quality of the job searches ...; (ii) consider any other matter that the Secretary considers relevant." (2):
-- for quality the Secretary "may have regard to" good faith, a variety of levels of seniority or pay, of fields and
-- occupations, and of methods. s 5: a "job search" is contact with a person or body "for the purposes of obtaining paid work".
DECLARE `My job search` IS ONE OF
    `not adequate: I did not make the number of job searches I was required to make (Job Search Efforts Determination s 6(1)(a))`
    `adequate on the number; the Secretary may still look at their quality (good faith, a variety of jobs, fields and methods) or other matters before deciding (s 6(1)(b), (2))`

@export Have I made "adequate job search efforts" for the period (s 42AC(1)(e), (3), Job Search Efforts Determination s 6)?
GIVEN `job searches I made` IS A NUMBER @desc How many job searches you made in the period (each contact with an employer or other person or body to get paid work counts, whether or not a job was advertised)
      `job searches I was required to make` IS A NUMBER @desc How many job searches you were required to make in the period
GIVETH A `My job search`
`Were my job search efforts adequate` MEANS
    IF `job searches I made` LESS THAN `job searches I was required to make`
    THEN `not adequate: I did not make the number of job searches I was required to make (Job Search Efforts Determination s 6(1)(a))`
    ELSE `adequate on the number; the Secretary may still look at their quality (good faith, a variety of jobs, fields and methods) or other matters before deciding (s 6(1)(b), (2))`

@export Is falling short on my required job searches a "mutual obligation failure" (ss 42AC(1)(e), (3))?
GIVEN `I receive a participation payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are receiving a participation payment
      `job searches I made` IS A NUMBER @desc How many job searches you made in the period
      `job searches I was required to make` IS A NUMBER @desc How many you were required to make
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my job search shortfall a mutual obligation failure` IF
        `job searches I made` LESS THAN `job searches I was required to make`
    AND `Have I committed a mutual obligation failure` `I receive a participation payment` `I did not satisfy the Secretary of adequate job search` FALSE FALSE

§§ `s 42AI, Reasonable Excuse Determination ss 5, 6 -- does my reason count`

-- s 5(2): the matters the Secretary "must take into account" in deciding whether a person has a reasonable excuse: (a) no
-- access to safe, secure and adequate housing, or using emergency accommodation or a refuge; (b) literacy and language skills;
-- (c) an illness, injury, impairment or disability; (d) a cognitive, neurological, psychiatric or psychological impairment or
-- mental illness; (e) a drug or alcohol dependency; (f) unforeseen family or caring responsibilities; (g) criminal violence
-- (including domestic violence and sexual assault); (h) the death of an immediate family member or close relative; (i)
-- undertaking paid work at the time; (j) attending a job interview at the time. s 6(3): not to be taken into account "if the
-- Secretary is not satisfied that the matter directly prevented the person from meeting the requirement". s 6(4): drug or
-- alcohol misuse or dependency is not taken into account where an earlier failure since 1 July 2018 was excused for it, the
-- person was referred to treatment and refused or failed to take part, unless (e) the treatment was unavailable or
-- inappropriate, (f) the person was genuinely unable to take part, (g) the person agreed and took all reasonable steps but it
-- did not start, or (h) the person had already completed the same or substantially similar treatment and a qualified medical
-- professional considers more would not help.
DECLARE `My reason` IS ONE OF
    `I had no safe, secure and adequate housing, or was in emergency accommodation or a refuge`
    `my literacy or language skills`
    `an illness, injury, impairment or disability`
    `a cognitive, neurological, psychiatric or psychological impairment, or mental illness`
    `a drug or alcohol dependency`
    `unforeseen family or caring responsibilities`
    `I was a victim of criminal violence, including domestic violence or sexual assault`
    `the death of an immediate family member or close relative`
    `I was at paid work at the time`
    `I was at a job interview at the time`
    `another reason`

DECLARE `How my reason counts` IS ONE OF
    `it is a matter the Secretary must take into account in deciding whether I had a reasonable excuse (Reasonable Excuse Determination s 5)`
    `it must not be taken into account: the Secretary is not satisfied it directly prevented me from meeting the requirement (s 6(3))`
    `it must not be taken into account: an earlier failure was excused for drug or alcohol dependency and I refused or failed to take part in the treatment I was referred to (s 6(4))`
    `it is not one of the listed matters; the Secretary may still consider it, since the list is of matters that must be taken into account`

@export I missed an appointment or activity. Does my reason have to be taken into account as a "reasonable excuse" (s 42AI, Reasonable Excuse Determination ss 5, 6)?
GIVEN `reason` IS A `My reason` @desc The reason you missed the requirement
      `the Secretary accepts it directly prevented me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary is satisfied the reason directly prevented you from meeting the requirement at the time (the Secretary decides)
      `an earlier failure was excused for drugs or alcohol and I did not do the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For drug or alcohol dependency: whether an earlier failure (since 1 July 2018) was excused or carried no demerit because of it, you were referred to treatment, and you refused or failed to take part
      `the treatment exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For that case: whether the treatment was unavailable or inappropriate, you were genuinely unable to take part, you agreed and tried but it did not start, or you had already completed the same kind of treatment and a medical professional says more would not help
GIVETH A `How my reason counts`
`Does my reason count as a reasonable excuse matter` MEANS
    IF `reason` EQUALS `another reason`
    THEN `it is not one of the listed matters; the Secretary may still consider it, since the list is of matters that must be taken into account`
    ELSE IF (NOT `the Secretary accepts it directly prevented me`)
         THEN `it must not be taken into account: the Secretary is not satisfied it directly prevented me from meeting the requirement (s 6(3))`
         ELSE IF `reason` EQUALS `a drug or alcohol dependency` AND `an earlier failure was excused for drugs or alcohol and I did not do the treatment` AND (NOT `the treatment exception applies`)
              THEN `it must not be taken into account: an earlier failure was excused for drug or alcohol dependency and I refused or failed to take part in the treatment I was referred to (s 6(4))`
              ELSE `it is a matter the Secretary must take into account in deciding whether I had a reasonable excuse (Reasonable Excuse Determination s 5)`

§§ `s 42AR, Non-Compliance Determination ss 5, 6 -- have my failures become "persistent", and how much can be cut` -- arises only after demerits

-- "Active months" (s 4): 3 active months are 91 consecutive days, extended by days exempt from the activity test, days not
-- required to meet the employment pathway plan, a week for each half reduction, two weeks for each whole reduction, any
-- post-cancellation non-payment period and the time awaiting a DHS assessment, up to 12 months; 6 active months the same from
-- 182 days. The person states whether events fell within them.
-- s 5(1): the Secretary "must be satisfied that a person has persistently committed mutual obligation failures if: (a) the
-- relevant failure was committed within 3 active months beginning on" the day the DHS assessment is complete, where in any 6
-- active months the person committed "(i) at least 5 mutual obligation failures to which a demerit is attached; or (ii) 2, 3
-- or 4 ... where at least 1 ... was: (A) failing to attend a job interview; or (B) failing to act on a job opportunity ...; or
-- (C) ... acting in a manner [that] could result in an offer of employment not being made", and "(b) the person undergoes a DHS
-- assessment"; "or (b) in the 3 active months prior to the relevant failure, the person has committed at least 1 mutual
-- obligation failure without a reasonable excuse where the Secretary was satisfied that the person had persistently committed
-- mutual obligation failures." (5): the Secretary "must not be satisfied" if no failure with a demerit, or without a reasonable
-- excuse, in the 3 active months before the relevant failure. (6): nor where a demerit is reversed so the count falls short.
-- (Demerits reversed are not counted: the person states the count after reversals.)
GIVEN `demerits in 6 active months` IS A NUMBER
      `one was a job interview, job opportunity or job offer failure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the demerit threshold is met` IF
        `demerits in 6 active months` AT LEAST 5
    OR (`demerits in 6 active months` AT LEAST 2 AND `one was a job interview, job opportunity or job offer failure`)

@export Must the Secretary treat my mutual obligation failures as "persistent" (s 42AF(2)(a), Non-Compliance Determination s 5)?
GIVEN `demerits in 6 active months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many mutual obligation failures with a demerit you committed in a period of 6 active months, not counting demerits since reversed
      `one was a job interview, job opportunity or job offer failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one of them was failing to attend a job interview, failing to act on a job opportunity your provider asked you to, or acting so that a job offer would foreseeably not be made
      `my DHS assessment is complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Services Australia has completed the assessment of whether your employment pathway plan suits you, after those demerits (and the plan was found suitable, so the demerits stand)
      `this failure is within 3 active months of the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the failure now being decided was committed within 3 active months beginning on the day that assessment was completed
      `a failure in the last 3 active months was already found persistent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 3 active months before this failure, you committed a failure without a reasonable excuse for which the Secretary was satisfied your failures were persistent
      `a failure with a demerit, or without excuse, in the last 3 active months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 3 active months before this failure, you committed any mutual obligation failure with a demerit, or without a reasonable excuse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my failures persistent` IF
        `a failure with a demerit, or without excuse, in the last 3 active months`
    AND (    (`the demerit threshold is met` `demerits in 6 active months` `one was a job interview, job opportunity or job offer failure` AND `my DHS assessment is complete` AND `this failure is within 3 active months of the assessment`)
          OR `a failure in the last 3 active months was already found persistent`)

-- s 6(1): where the Secretary decides under s 42AF(2)(c) to reduce an instalment for persistent failures, "the Secretary must
-- determine that paragraph 42AN(3)(a) of the Act applies" (half an instalment). (2): the whole instalment (s 42AN(3)(b)) if, in
-- the 3 active months before the relevant failure, the Secretary's last s 42AF(2)(c) determination was a half reduction. (4):
-- back to half for "the first mutual obligation failure where the person does not have a reasonable excuse in the 3 active
-- months since" a s 42AF(2)(d) cancellation.
DECLARE `My reduction` IS ONE OF
    `half of one instalment (s 42AN(3)(a); Non-Compliance Determination s 6(1))`
    `the whole of one instalment (s 42AN(3)(b); s 6(2))`
    `half of one instalment: the first failure after my payment was cancelled (s 6(4))`

@export If the Secretary reduces my participation payment for persistent failures, by how much (s 42AN, Non-Compliance Determination s 6)?
GIVEN `my last reduction in the last 3 active months was a half` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 3 active months before this failure, the Secretary's most recent reduction for persistent failures was a half-instalment reduction
      `this is my first failure since a cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your payment was cancelled for persistent failures and this is your first failure without a reasonable excuse in the 3 active months since
GIVETH A `My reduction`
`How much can my instalment be cut` MEANS
    IF `this is my first failure since a cancellation`
    THEN `half of one instalment: the first failure after my payment was cancelled (s 6(4))`
    ELSE IF `my last reduction in the last 3 active months was a half`
         THEN `the whole of one instalment (s 42AN(3)(b); s 6(2))`
         ELSE `half of one instalment (s 42AN(3)(a); Non-Compliance Determination s 6(1))`
